{
  "_doc": "EXP-1145: a PLAIN Merge control on a member of a PR stack asks first, x4 (web lib/pr-stack.ts stackMergeChoice; desktop pr_stack::stack_merge_choice; iOS PrStack.stackMergeChoice; Android PrStack.stackMergeChoice). Input: the issue being merged + the synced issue rows (id, identifier, branch, prBaseBranch, prState, prUrl). Only OPEN pull requests form the chain (stackChain over the open rows in identifier order); choice is null when the issue has no open PR or its chain has fewer than 2 open members -> merge plainly, no dialog. Otherwise the dialog: title, listing (members bottom to top joined by ' → ', the merged one suffixed ' (this one)', a batch PR named 'EXP-2 +1'), the two sentences, body = listing + blank line + stackSentence + newline + thisSentence; buttons mergeStack (issues.mergePr({issueId: topIssueId, mergeStack: true})), mergeThis (the plain single-PR merge), cancel. SLOP-3: Reviews rows ask the same way. LEGACY since EXP-1248: `labels` + `cases` stay only until the natives port `confirm` (wave B), then they go.",
  "confirm": {
    "_doc": "EXP-1248: the ONE stack merge confirm x4 (web lib/pr-stack.ts stackMergeConfirm; desktop pr_stack::stack_merge_confirm; iOS PrStack.stackMergeConfirm; Android PrStack.stackMergeConfirm). It replaces the 3-way dialog. Input: the issue, the synced issue rows (id, identifier, branch, prBaseBranch, prState, prUrl) and a mode: 'stack' = the ONE merge control, labelled Merge stack on any member of an open stack (lands the whole open chain: input = the TOP member), 'through' = the ghost Merge through here on a hovered stack-rail row / a phone row's long-press (lands that member and every open member beneath it: input = that issue). Only a LINEAR open stack of 2+ pull requests (pr-stack-view.json rules: open rows, one representative per pr_url, no fork) has one; null = the plain merge confirm. title = the primary button = contract diffUi.mergeStack / diffUi.mergeThrough; landing = bottom-first labels (a batch PR = 'EXP-2 +1'); staysOpen = the members above (GitHub retargets them); body = 'Lands 1 pull request: X.' or 'Lands N pull requests, bottom-up: A, B.' plus ' C stays open.' / ' C, D stay open.' when any; input = issues.mergePr({issueId, mergeStack: true}). Server: mergeStack = ONE GitHub merge-async on that member after the line is made a GitHub stack (no fallback).",
